\image{conf-alphastim-ces-gad.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} A double-blind RCT of at-home \strong{cranial electrotherapy stimulation (Alpha-Stim AID)} for generalized anxiety disorder in young adults, with resting-state HD-EEG as a mechanistic readout. Active CES reduced frontal-midline theta power and Default-Mode-Network alpha connectivity, and those EEG changes correlated with self-reported somatic-anxiety improvement — offered as the first neurophysiological evidence of a CES mechanism for GAD.}
